  "cause": "**In twenty-four hours Russia struck a village aid queue, a hospice and a hospital, and Kyiv lost its water.** The **BBC** reports at least **38 civilians killed** and scores wounded across strikes in the last 24 hours. At least **33** are known dead in **Komyshuvakha**, in the southern **Zaporizhzhia** region, where **nine 3,000kg glide bombs** hit on Monday night as residents gathered at a school used for weekly humanitarian distributions. **President Zelensky** called it *\"one of the largest mass killings committed by Russia during this war\"* and said **more than 50 people** could still be trapped; regional head **Mykhailo Semikin** said *\"the scale of the tragedy is difficult to comprehend\"*. Local media reported that people took refuge underground when the attack began, and that the **roof collapsed** on them. Russia's defence ministry said the strike targeted Ukrainian military units and killed **25 servicemen**; the BBC's Russian defence correspondent **Ilya Abishev** reports there is **no credible evidence** the site was used by the military and **no major military or industrial facilities** in the settlement — though the village sits on the defensive and transport network approaching the regional capital. **The same night, the targets were people who could not be evacuated.** In **Dnipro** a missile destroyed a hospice and roughly **50 terminally ill patients** were being moved to other facilities, the oldest **90**. Mayor **Boris Filatov** posted photographs of elderly people in beds amid blown-out windows and rubble, writing: *\"I realise that I am violating ethics… I want as many people as possible to see these photos. Especially politicians and diplomats. Especially abroad. These are elderly, terminally ill people. This is a Russian missile.\"* A separate Dnipro strike killed two and wounded 18. In **Kharkiv** a hospital was hit and **73 people wounded**, most of them elderly patients. Five more were killed in Donetsk region. Russia also struck **energy infrastructure in nine regions**; the capital's water supplier **Kyivvodokanal** said supply to **Kyiv was entirely cut off** by damage to energy infrastructure, the **entire metro was suspended** on Tuesday, and Mayor **Vitali Klitschko** said the power situation was becoming *\"very difficult\"*. **And on the day of the largest mass killing, the Kremlin announced a table.** Three-way talks with Ukraine, brokered by the **US**, will be held in **Abu Dhabi on 10–11 November** — the first trilateral meeting since **February**. Since then Washington and Moscow have dealt with each other more directly, including a Trump-announced deal to **import Russian diesel**.",
