  "verse": "Already the ‹Teaching of the Prophets› that has been given since time immemorial speaks of these things and that you shall defend yourselves against these might-greedy machinations of the authorities and mightful ones, so that fairness, responsibility and conscientiousness may prevail amongst all peoples, yes amongst your entire humankind, so that true love may spread all around amongst you human beings and there may be peace, freedom and harmony in the human being and on the whole world.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 22, Verse 24",
  "hinge": "The cause is not the hacker. It is the decision — by manufacturers, whether a fridge that loses its network fails safe or obeys whatever is on the other end; by retailers, whether \"physical modification\" is a project with a completion date or a line in a risk register; by governments, whether a controller sold to a shop and a controller sold to a base are covered by one standard; and by the agencies now monitoring, whether they publish what they find before the fourth wave. §22:24 asks for \"responsibility and conscientiousness\" precisely because the alternative is what Horne described: a technology base nobody invested in, defended by advice to people who are told the choice is theirs. The choice is theirs. That is the cause, and it is the thing that can be changed this month rather than after the next defrosting."
